                }
              ],
              "text": "4:00 AM. The regular check-in reports the battery at **20%**. That is the low-battery line, so the Kestrel cloud marks the camera low and sends **one** \"Porch Cam battery low\" alert. It will not send another until the battery is back above 30%. This is the alert a customer asks about in the morning.",
              "panels": {
                "batt": {
                  "charge": 20,
                  "note": "reported 20% · low-battery alert sent"
                },
                "app": {
                  "notify": {
                    "app": "Kestrel",
                    "title": "Porch Cam battery low",
                    "text": "Battery at 20%"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "sunrise",
              "time": "06:50",
              "nodes": [
                "cam"
              ],
              "text": "6:50 AM. Sunrise. The small solar panel starts charging the battery. Nobody is told yet: the camera will say it is charging at its next check-in.",
              "panels": {
